  "Notes": [
    "Tutorial assumptions, not a fitted material or experimental validation.",
    "All pressures are absolute. Velocity inputs are interstitial at the inlet gas pressure and temperature.",
    "Bed length is packed length; diameter is internal. The assumed wall thickness is 2 mm.",
    "Two complete cycles show startup; this is not a claim of cyclic steady state or grid convergence.",
    "See examples/SIZING.md for flow, inventory, timing, mesh and equipment assumptions.",
    "Isothermal feature tutorial, not a DAC or material-validation case. Feed contains 10 mol% CO2 to show a front within tutorial-scale simulated time; N2 is nonadsorbing.",
    "CO2 moisture-swing Langmuir and H2O GAB parameters are illustrative. SPI is required for these RH-dependent empirical isotherms.",
    "At 298.15 K the code gives water saturation pressure 3169.824486 Pa. Source H2O fractions are RH*psat/P: 10% RH during adsorption/drying and 80% during wet release.",
    "Wet purge contains 10 mol% CO2, so its CO2 is external input and must be included in a capture balance. Drying purge contains 1 mol% CO2; its exhaust is recorded separately.",
    "Every source and the initial bed contain positive water. Do not use exact zero RH with the logarithmic moisture-swing model in v0.4.1.",
    "MSA changes humidity at 1 bar; MVSA additionally regenerates at 0.2 bar. Wet-source water fraction is recalculated at that pressure.",
    "Vacuum drying precedes repressurization. The drying source has 10% RH at 0.2 bar; its H2O fraction is recalculated for that pressure. Drying velocity is -0.05 m/s.",
    "One-way exhaust valves prevent backfilling from the vacuum receiver. Exhaust and repressurization are capped at 0.003 mol/s. The adsorption outlet valve is sized for the nominal 0.00158413 mol/s at a 1 kPa drop to a 0.99 bar header.",
    "Source humidity is specified; local bed RH is transported and can differ from the source value. Check RH together with pressure, especially during evacuation and repressurization.",
    "The repressurization source preserves the vacuum-drying gas mole fractions. Its specified RH is therefore 50% at 1 bar (the same mixture was 10% RH at 0.2 bar); local RH changes with pressure and water uptake. This avoids imposing an extra drying shock at the start of filling.",
    "REPRESS ends at mean pressure >= 0.99 bar and pressure nonuniformity <= 0.02, after at least 1 s; failure to reach the endpoint within 60 s is an error. This avoids holding at an asymptotically closed source valve."
  ],
